  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Girls in Education Dialogue</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Girls in Education Dialogue (GED) project was established by MAYEIN IN 2022 to train schoolgirls across urban and peri-urban areas in Oyo State to become self-advocates and exercise their agency in education decision-making. This training is then followed by initiating a series of formal dialogues between school girls and stakeholders &#x2013; spanning parents, teachers, school supervisors, community leaders, and Ministry of Education officials - which experientially model how to best communicate with girlsin education system planning, implementation, and evaluation respectively. It will culminate in a Schoolgirls General Assembly where schoolgirl delegates will make parliamentary-style presentations before a presiding committee of education decision-makers. The participants of this program, undergo training on capacity building and advocacy, which covers training on leadership, public speaking, financial literacy, and effective communication.

The Girls in Education Dialogues (GED) Project, launched by MAYEIN in 2022, fosters direct engagement between schoolgirls and education decision-makers in Oyo State. It includes capacity-building for 100 girls through trained facilitators, state-level dialogues with key stakeholders like PTA groups, school principals, and policymakers, and culminates in the OyoState Schoolgirls General Assembly (OYSGA). There, 10 schoolgirl delegates from 10 schools advocate for girls&apos; education improvements before the State Commissioners of Education and other high-level decision-makers.</narrative>
  </description>
