  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mentoring Assistance for Youths and Entrepreneurs Initiative (MAYEIN), a non-governmental organization headquartered in Oyo State, Nigeria, focuses on Positive Youth Development through the strategic advancement of SDGs 4, 5, 16, and 17. Established formally in May 2012, with registration No: CAC/IT/NO 52811, the Organization is governed by an 8-member Board of Trustees and advisory committee. MAYEIN has grown from its nascent stages of budding systems into a thriving and well-structured professional organization with 2 office locations and a community outstation in Oyo State. The Organization currently has 8 employees, 10 volunteers across several local governments, and 5 NGO implementation partners in different states in Nigeria. Our organization has also recorded significant local donors and major internal grant partners &#x2013; including the Queen&#x2019;s Commonwealth Trust, United Kingdom (2020 &#x2013; 2022), and Rockefeller Philanthropy, USA (2022). Since 2012, MAYEIN has impacted over 20,000 youth across Nigeria through a compendium of programs, campaigns, and direct services. Our main approaches to impact include research and learning, flexible spaces, partnerships, and mentoring.

Vision: We envision a country and continent where young people are thriving in their communities and correspondingly communitiesare thriving because of young people

Mission: To lead strategies that promote inclusive and qualitative education and lifelong learning for all, gender equity, and civic readiness for attaining positive youth development and future readiness.</narrative>
